{
  "dom_id": "step-e451",
  "name": "Example: Integrating a Combination of Linear Rational Functions Using the General Formula",
  "problem": "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int\\left(\\dfrac{1}{1+2x} + \\dfrac{1}{1-2x}\\right)\\,\\textrm d x.$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's solve this using the general formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{1}{1+2x}+\\frac{1}{1-2x})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{1+2x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{1-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|1+2x|-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|1-2x|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|\\frac{1+2x}{1-2x}|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061K \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(K|\\frac{1+2x}{1-2x}|)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we used the laws of logarithms to write the result as a single logarithm.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
